The skill level with the second weapon isn't very important.
IIRC you chances to hit are dependent on the lower of
two-weapon skill and primary weapon skill. If the primary
hits the secondary automatically hits. So raising saber to
basic is worth +2 damage. The saber is handy in the VotD,
lots of vampires and demons, and Ghost Town, vampires,
demons and shades. It's worth +d20 when it sears their flesh
and you can't damage a shade without silver.

